    {
      "section": "dsh-vaultwarden",
      "text": "English | [中文](README.md)\n\nA **Vaultwarden / Bitwarden** integration for DeepSeek Harness. Browse and edit the vault from **Settings → Password vault**, and let models search, read and write entries on demand. Passwords, TOTP codes and card data are masked with stable placeholders by default, and plaintext in local session logs can be scrubbed. Works with self-hosted Vaultwarden and Bitwarden Cloud."
    },
    {
      "section": "Preview",
      "text": "| Password vault | Masking trail |\n| --- | --- |\n|  |  |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Highlights",
      "text": "- **Real-time sync & cache**: SignalR WebSocket updates, with automatic polling fallback and upgrade retries; an encrypted local cache plus revision probing speeds up cold starts.\n- **Vault panel**: sections, search, paging, entry details, TOTP countdown, copy, create/edit, archive/trash/restore and folder moves; write actions follow the plugin's access tier.\n- **Masking & log scrubbing**: passwords, TOTP codes and card data are returned as stable placeholders, fetchable per entry and field; plaintext in session logs is periodically replaced with `[REDACTED:BW]`, with incremental and immediate sweeps.\n- **Masking dashboard**: daily totals, top conversations/models and a drill-down masking ledger.\n- **Passkeys**: read passkey metadata from entries; export a 0600 WebAuthn credential file under the plugin's access tier (v2 with `cdp` and `playwright` blocks for CDP clients and Playwright), with import, remove and temporary-file cleanup; login recipe in [docs/passkey-login.md](docs/passkey-login.md).\n- **Permissions & security**: read-only / ask / full-access tiers; when the DSH session is `workspace-write` or `read-only`, writes and passkey exports still go through host approval. The "
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```sh"
    },
    {
      "section": "Latest stable tarball used by the marketplace",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web add https://github.com/BuvkB/dsh-vaultwarden/releases/latest/download/dsh-vaultwarden.tgz"
    },
    {
      "section": "Or from npm",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web add dsh-vaultwarden@latest\n```\n\nRequires Node.js >= 22."
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "| Field | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| `serverUrl` / `email` | Vaultwarden URL and login email |\n| `masterPassword` | Master password; write-only |\n| `apiKeyClientId` / `apiKeyClientSecret` | Optional API-key login (bypasses two-factor prompts) |\n| `accessMode` | `readonly` / `ask` / `auto` for model-driven writes |\n| `maskEnabled` | Plugin masking master switch (on by default). Off returns plaintext, hides the masking trail page and stops log scrubbing; turn it off only when another local masking service already covers this path |\n| `sweepMode` | Log-scrubbing switch (subject to `maskEnabled`) |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "When the DSH session is `workspace-write` / `read-only` (`approval: ask`), writes and passkey exports still require host approval even if the plugin is set to `auto`. Password/TOTP reads, log scrubbing and passkey temporary-file cleanup do not require approval; the latter two are forced security cleanups.\n\n`DSH_BITWARDEN_*` environment variables and profile composition are also supported. See [docs/ui-design.md](docs/ui-design.md) for every field."
